  "insights": [
    "Total clinical admissions logged across FY2024 reached 4,000 patients with an average hospital stay of 7.45 days (median: 7 days).",
    "Cardiovascular Diseases represent the highest single diagnostic burden (862 admissions, 21.6%), followed closely by Respiratory Infections (669 admissions).",
    "Emergency admissions constitute 53.8% of total hospital intake (2,151 patients), indicating high acute-care dependence.",
    "Departmental operational load is led by Cardiology (786 patients, 19.7%), followed by Pulmonology (598 patients).",
    "Length of Stay (LOS) varies significantly by operational unit: Intensive Care Unit (ICU) exhibits the longest average stay (13.86 days), whereas Endocrinology maintains the most rapid turnaround (4.96 days).",
    "Senior (56-70) and Geriatric (71+) cohorts together account for 49.0% of total bed-days, with Cardiovascular conditions predominating in both cohorts.",
    "Oncology & Neoplasms exhibits the highest condition-specific length of stay (9.97 days average), reflecting extensive chemotherapy and post-surgical monitoring regimens.",
    "Total financial volume generated across all episodes is \u20b9269,334,523 (average \u20b967,333 per admission episode) with 48% private comprehensive insurance coverage."
